From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 01:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm: h713-afbd: do not vmap PRIME imports

The driver declares DRM_GEM_DMA_DRIVER_OPS_VMAP, whose only effect over the
plain variant is to use drm_gem_dma_prime_import_sg_table_vmap() -- so every
imported dma-buf is CPU-vmapped and the pointer stored in dma_obj->vaddr.
drm_gem_dma_free() then vunmaps it when the handle is closed.

Nothing imported PRIME buffers into this driver until the NV12 video plane, so
that was inert. With the plane it is a kernel BUG. Importing a dma-buf exported
by sunxi-scanout-dmabuf and closing the handle gives:

  kernel BUG at drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c:1589!
    dma_buf_vunmap_unlocked
    drm_gem_dma_free
    drm_gem_object_handle_put_unlocked
    drm_gem_handle_delete
    drm_gem_close_ioctl

Line 1589 is BUG_ON(!iosys_map_is_equal(&dmabuf->vmap_ptr, map)): the exporter
does not record a vmap matching the vaddr the importer cached.

A scanout plane needs the buffer's DMA address, not a CPU mapping, so the vmap
was never wanted. Drop it. dumb_create is identical between the two macros, so
fbdev/fbcon on the primary plane is unaffected -- those buffers are allocated
rather than imported and get their vaddr from drm_gem_dma_create().

Fixes the crash without touching the exporter, which is the smaller and more
correct half of the contract.

Applies after 0078.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
@@ -506,7 +506,7 @@
 static const struct drm_driver h713_afbd_driver = {
 	.driver_features	= DRIVER_GEM | DRIVER_MODESET | DRIVER_ATOMIC,
 	.fops			= &h713_afbd_fops,
-	DRM_GEM_DMA_DRIVER_OPS_VMAP,
+	DRM_GEM_DMA_DRIVER_OPS,
 	DRM_FBDEV_DMA_DRIVER_OPS,
 	.name			= "sun50i-h713-afbd",
 	.desc			= "Allwinner H713 AFBD scanout",
